#
# PAM service stack for rdpd / rdp-sessionmgr.
#
# Install at /etc/pam.d/rdpd and pass `-S rdpd` to rdp-sessionmgr.
# Without this file, the daemon defaults to the universally-present
# "login" service.  Tailor the stack to taste (e.g. add pam_faillock
# for lockouts, pam_access for ACLs). The session stack runs around
# every RDP login, so pam_limits, pam_loginuid or pam_systemd can be
# added there as on a console login.
#
auth      required   pam_unix.so          nullok_secure
account   required   pam_unix.so
session   required   pam_unix.so
password  required   pam_unix.so
